cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. Please also cite the connectome data (FlyWire / FAFB, MCNS, BANC, hemibrain, MANC) and the cell-type annotations it builds on."
title: "flybrain: code and results for 'Typing the rare neurons of an unlabeled connectome by graph matching, guided by a transferred graph neural network'"
abstract: >-
  Code, protocols and result summaries for typing the rare neurons of an
  unlabeled Drosophila connectome. A graph neural network that sees only
  anonymous wiring is transferred from an annotated connectome without target
  labels and selects candidate neurons; graph matching against the reference's
  rare-type neurons assigns their types. Tested under pre-registered protocols
  on the BANC brain (rare-type accuracy 22 to 41 %) and, from MANC, on the
  nerve cords of BANC and the male CNS (40 to 61 % and 72 to 82 %). A
  pre-specified analysis on BANC compares and combines wiring with automatic
  morphology matches (NBLAST).
